In this subsection we describe how to generate the virtual bones given the simulation sequence of garments 𝐺 ˆ {1 , 2,...,𝑡 }  
. Similar to TailorNet [Patel et al . 2020], our method decomposes the garment meshes to the low-frequency and the high-frequency deformations.
Given a garment mesh 𝐺 ˆ , we perform Laplacian smoothing to obtain a smoothed mesh, which can be treated as the low-frequency deformation 𝐺 ˆ 𝐿𝐹 , and take the residual as the high-frequency deformation 𝐺 ˆ 𝐻𝐹 = 𝐺 ˆ − 𝐺 ˆ 𝐿𝐹 .
